1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Key's in the ignition. It won't turn.
The wheel feels locked solid.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Before you assume the ignition's dead,
this can be a lot simpler.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Most cars have an anti-theft steering lock.
Turn the wheel with the key out, it can clamp down.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
One clue it's the lock: gently rock the wheel
side to side while easing the key. Do not force it.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
On push-button start cars, a weak fob or
12-volt battery can also block the release.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
If it's not the lock, don't guess at the part.
Stop by and we'll take a look. Nick's Tire and Auto.
